"Please build a strategy deck storyline for the following brief.\n\nAudience: CEO and CFO of Caraway Infrastructure Group, a civil infrastructure contractor\nDecision: whether to pursue a bid for the Northgate Expressway rehabilitation contract (estimated value $280M over 4 years)\n\n---\n**CARAWAY INFRASTRUCTURE — NORTHGATE BID DECISION BRIEF**\n\nNorthgate Expressway is a 47-mile toll expressway in the Pacific Northwest operated by the Northgate Transit Authority (NTA). NTA issued an RFQ in October 2026 for a 4-year rehabilitation contract (pavement resurfacing, bridge deck repairs, drainage systems) estimated at $280M total contract value.\n\nCaraway's position:\n- Caraway has completed 3 comparable expressway rehabilitation contracts in the past 5 years ($140M, $95M, $190M)\n- Caraway's current backlog: $310M across 7 active contracts\n- Current workforce utilization: 91% of field capacity committed through Q2 2027\n- Estimated bid cost: $1.4M (design, estimating, proposal preparation)\n- Win probability (internal estimate): 35%\n- If won, contract would begin mobilization in Q4 2027 and run through Q4 2031\n\nFinancial projections if won:\n- Gross revenue: $280M over 4 years (~$70M/year)\n- Projected gross margin: 11% ($30.8M over 4 years)\n- Projected EBIT: 7% ($19.6M over 4 years; average $4.9M/year)\n- Caraway FY2025 revenue: $218M; FY2026 projected revenue: $247M\n\nCapacity note: The contract requires peak mobilization of 340 field personnel. Caraway currently has 290 field personnel. The gap of 50 is expected to be filled through a combination of permanent hiring (30) and subcontracting (20). The hiring timeline requires starting recruitment in Q1 2027 for a Q4 2027 mobilization.\n\nCompetitive context: NTA has pre-qualified 4 bidders. Industry sources suggest Westfall Civil (a larger regional competitor) is the likely frontrunner due to a prior NTA relationship.\n\nFootnote 1: Caraway's 91% field utilization figure is measured as of October 2026. Three contracts in the current backlog reach substantial completion in Q1–Q2 2027, which will reduce utilization to approximately 67% by Q3 2027 — before Northgate mobilization would begin.\n\nFootnote 2: The 35% win probability is the business development team's estimate. The CEO's prior view, expressed in the September 2027 strategy retreat, was that Caraway should not pursue contracts where it is not in the top two positions of the competitive field. With Westfall Civil as likely frontrunner, Caraway is likely bidding for second or third position.\n\n---\nFull storyline please."